{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_20260524004151454d3e9654234a55","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-5.1","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I don't see a \"create-app\" or \"create-game\" command in tma. The `create` command is for creating a project locally, not creating an app on the platform. So I'll need to create the game through the developer console UI or through the API directly.\n\nLet me try using the API approach. I have the tma cookies which work for microapp.bytedance.com. Let me try to use them to call the Douyin API to create a new game.\n\nActually, let me think about this differently. The Douyin developer platform at developer.open-douyin.com uses a different authentication system from microapp.bytedance.com. However, the old API endpoints at developer.toutiao.com use the same auth as tma.\n\nLet me try to:\n1. Use curl with the tma cookies to call the old API\n2. See if I can create a game that way\n\nOr, let me try using Playwright to:\n1. Launch Chromium with the tma cookies\n2. Navigate to open-douyin.com\n3. Try the SSO login flow\n\nActually, I just realized something. Let me try to use Playwright to launch Edge with the user's profile directory. Even though the cookies file wasn't found at the exact path I checked, the user's Edge profile might be at a different location.\n\nLet me check the Edge profile location.\n\nActually, let me try a simpler approach first. Let me see if I can use the microapp.bytedance.com cookies to access the open-douyin.com developer console through SSO.\n\nThe SSO flow would be:\n1. Navigate to developer.open-douyin.com\n2. It should redirect to a login page\n3. If I have microapp.bytedance.com cookies, the SSO might work\n\nLet me try writing a Playwright script to do this.\n\nActually, looking at the workflow document again:\n> 用Playwright设置open-douyin.com cookies→访问`developer.open-douyin.com/login-check?service=https://microapp.bytedance.com/`→获取microapp.bytedance.com cookies\n\nThis