{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_20260524004215cdec5445bf8945e4","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-5.1","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The Edge cookies file seems to be the newer encrypted format (Extension Cookies). Let me try a different approach.\n\nLet me use Playwright to launch Chromium with the cookies from tma session. I'll write a script that:\n1. Sets the microapp.bytedance.com cookies in Playwright\n2. Tries to access developer.open-douyin.com through SSO\n\nOr better yet, let me try to use the old developer API (developer.toutiao.com) with the tma cookies to create a new game. This might be easier.\n\nLet me check if there's an API to create a game on developer.toutiao.com.\n\nActually, let me take a step back. The key insight from the workflow document is:\n> **新旧平台认证不互通**：CLI(tmg/tma)用 developer.toutiao.com 认证，新版控制台用 developer.open-douyin.com\n\nSo the old API (developer.toutiao.com) and the new console (developer.open-douyin.com) have separate auth. The tma cookies work for the old API.\n\nLet me try to use the old API to create a game. Let me search for the API endpoint.\n\nActually, I think the best approach is:\n1. Write a Playwright script that launches Chromium\n2. Sets the microapp.bytedance.com cookies\n3. Navigates to developer.open-douyin.com/login-check\n4. The SSO should authenticate us\n5. Then navigate to the game creation page\n6. Create the game\n\nLet me write this script.\n\nWait, but the login-check URL in the workflow goes FROM open-douyin TO microapp.bytedance.com:\n> 访问`developer.open-douyin.com/login-check?service=https://microapp.bytedance.com/`→获取microapp.bytedance.com cookies\n\nThis means: if you have open-douyin.com cookies, visiting this URL gives you microapp.bytedance.com cookies.\n\nFor the REVERSE direction (microapp.bytedance.com → open-douyin.com), I need to find the right URL.\n\nActually, let me try the SSO approach differently. Let me:\n1. Launch Playwright Chromium\n2. Set cookies for microapp.bytedance.com\n3. Navigate to developer.open-douyin.com\n4. Check if we get redirected to login or if SSO works\n\nLet me try this with a quick script.\n\nActually, let me think about this differently. The old developer platform at developer.toutiao.com uses the same auth as tma. Let me try to create a game through the old platform API.\n\nThe old platform should have an API for creating apps. Let me try:\n1. Use curl with the tma cookies\n2. POST to the create app API on developer.toutiao.com\n\nLet me try to find the right API endpoint.\n\nActually, let me just write a comprehensive Playwright script that:\n1. Launches Chromium\n2. Adds the tma cookies for microapp.bytedance.com domain\n3. Tries to SSO into developer.open-douyin.com\n4. Creates the game\n\nLet me write this script now.\n\nActually, let me try a simpler approach first - let me check if there's a way to create an app through the old API at developer.toutiao.com.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1f456d29-d84c-44e0-89e7-7ad362d1b1bb","uuid":"d58d22e2-ec6d-46a2-ab6d-150be7455cc0"}
