{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_202605240044024b3d61323a3a4f38","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-5.1","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Got 403 from the old API. The cookies might not have the right CSRF tokens. Let me try a different approach.\n\nLet me try using Playwright more effectively. I'll:\n1. Launch a browser with the tma cookies\n2. Navigate to the login page on open-douyin.com\n3. Try the phone/SMS login or SSO flow\n4. Create the game\n\nActually, let me think about this differently. The task says:\n> 用Playwright连接Edge浏览器(SSO cookie转换方案参考D:/loopcli/main/memory/facts/douyin-publish-workflow.md)登录developer.open-douyin.com\n\nThe SSO cookie conversion approach mentioned goes FROM open-douyin.com TO microapp.bytedance.com. But for this task, I need to go FROM microapp.bytedance.com TO open-douyin.com.\n\nWait, let me re-read the approach:\n> 用Playwright设置open-douyin.com cookies→访问`developer.open-douyin.com/login-check?service=https://microapp.bytedance.com/`→获取microapp.bytedance.com cookies\n\nSo the original approach was:\n1. Get open-douyin.com cookies (from the user's Edge browser via Playwright CDP)\n2. Use those to get microapp.bytedance.com cookies\n3. Use microapp cookies for tma\n\nFor this task, the flow would be reversed - I need open-douyin.com cookies to access the developer console. But I don't have them.\n\nLet me try to:\n1. Launch Edge with Playwright using the user's profile\n2. Navigate to open-douyin.com\n3. The user should be logged in from their previous session\n\nLet me try this approach. I'll launch Edge (not Chromium) with the user profile.\n\nActually, from the previous task's experience:\n> Edge cookie v20 加密是 app-bound，无法从外部解密\n> Playwright 可通过 CDP 连接用户 Edge 浏览器，获取 open-douyin.com 的认证\n\nSo the approach was to connect to an already running Edge browser via CDP. But the user's Edge browser needs to be running with remote debugging enabled.\n\nLet me try to:\n1. Launch Edge with remote debugging por