m.\n\nThe proper SSO flow should be:\n1. User is logged in on open-douyin.com\n2. Visit login-check URL which validates the open-douyin.com session\n3. If valid, sets cookies on microapp.bytedance.com and redirects there\n\nBut the login-check is redirecting to the login page, meaning the open-douyin.com session is no longer valid for this SSO flow.\n\nLet me try a different approach. Let me navigate to the login-check URL from the open-douyin.com console page (where we're already logged in) instead of going directly.\n\nActually, I think the issue is that the page I opened navigated away from the open-douyin.com session. Let me try navigating directly to the login-check URL from a page that has the open-douyin.com cookies set.\n\nWait, actually the cookies ARE set (44 cookies from open-douyin.com). But the login-check is still redirecting to login. This might be because the login-check requires a specific cookie or session state.\n\nLet me try to use the previous approach that worked: set open-douyin.com cookies in a new browser context, then visit login-check.\n\nActually, looking at the original cookie string from before:\n```\ncsrf_session_id=...; passport_csrf_token=...; sid_guard_microapp=...; uid_tt_microapp=...; ...\n```\n\nThese cookies all have `_microapp` suffix, meaning they were for microapp.bytedance.com. The open-douyin.com cookies don't have these suffixes.\n\nThe previous SSO conversion must have been done differently. Let me try:\n1. Open a page on open-douyin.com first (where the user is logged in)\n2. Then navigate to the login-check URL\n3. This should pass through the SSO properly","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1f456d29-d84c-44e0-89e7-7ad362d1b1bb","uuid":"6c0520df-3d66-48ba-a4a2-7282205585df"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_20260524012038a7efb41e04794ff1","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-5.1","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_15524f8ae6ad4a68ab197157","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat > /tmp/sso_convert.cjs << 'ENDSCRIPT'\nconst { chromium } = require('playwright');\nconst fs = require('fs');\n(async () => {\n  const browser = await chromium.connectOverCDP('http://127.0.0.1:9222');\n  const context = browser.contexts()[0];\n  \n  // First, go to open-douyin.com to establish the session\n  const page = await context.newPage();\n  console.log('Step 1: Navigate to open-douyin.com...');\n  await page.goto('https://developer.open-douyin.com/console', {\n    waitUntil: 'domcontentloaded', timeout: 30000\n  });\n  await page.waitForTimeout(5000);\n  console.log('URL:', page.url());\n  \n  // Check if logged in\n  const text = await page.evaluate(() => document.body.innerText.substring(0, 500));\n  const isLoggedIn = text.includes('控制台') || text.includes('uunderlie');\n  console.log('Logged in on open-douyin.com:', isLoggedIn);\n  \n  if (!isLoggedIn) {\n    console.log('Not logged in, aborting');\n    await browser.close();\n    return;\n  }\n  \n  // Now navigate to login-check URL\n  console.log('Step 2: Navigate to login-check...');\n  await page.goto('https://developer.open-douyin.com/login-check?service=https://microapp.bytedance.com/', {\n    waitUntil: 'domcontentloaded', timeout: 30000\n  });\n  await page.waitForTimeout(5000);\n  console.log('URL after login-check:', page.url());\n  \n  // Get microapp.bytedance.com cookies\n  const cookies = await context.cookies(['https://microapp.bytedance.com']);\n  console.log('microapp cookies:', cookies.length);\n  \n  // Filter for session-related cookies\n  const sessionCookies = cookies.filter(c => \n    c.name.includes('session') || c.name.includes('sid') || c.name.includes('uid') || \n    c.name.includes('csrf') || c.name.includes('passport')\n  );\n  console.log('Session